cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these estimates, this pipeline, or the published dataset, please cite the work below."
title: "Equity Analysis at a Large Scale: Using Small Area Estimation to Get the Most from the CRDC School Arrest Data"
abstract: >-
  Bayesian small-area estimates of school-based arrest rates from the US
  Department of Education's Civil Rights Data Collection (2015-16, 2017-18, and
  2021-22). School-based arrests are rare and unevenly reported: the most common
  district count is zero, and a classical confidence interval around a rare rate
  is too wide to compare districts with. We fit ten Bayesian hierarchical
  specifications and show that small area estimation narrows those intervals
  substantially while improving coverage, making it possible to say which
  differences between student groups, places, and years are real. This
  repository contains the full pipeline together with the published API and
  open dataset.
type: software
